## What Should Be Sent Back

Based on the OpenRouter docs I found, annotations CAN be passed back (evidenced by the PDF preservation feature). The format should be:

```json
{
  "role": "assistant",
  "content": "The 31st prime number is 127 [prime-numbers.info](https://...)",
  "annotations": [
    {
      "type": "url_citation",
      "url_citation": {
        "url": "https://prime-numbers.info/number/31st-prime",
        "title": "31st prime is 127",
        "content": "31st prime is 127. [127]...",
        "start_index": 0,
        "end_index": 0
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

We need to:
1. **Convert Greger citations back to OpenRouter annotations** when building the request
2. **Keep the inline citation links** (like `[prime-numbers.info](https://...)`) in the text

This way the conversation is fully reproducible - OpenRouter gets back the same annotation structure it sent, just like with `reasoning_details`.

